{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["Let there be lights (מארת) — it is the way of Scripture to use a singular form with a plural meaning, as in ״ויהי אנשים אשר היו טמאים״. And so its meaning is: let there be the making of — and what is it? Of lights (מאורות)." "In the firmament of the heavens — the beaten-out surface (הנרקע). And its meaning is: beneath the upper heavens." "In the firmament (ברקיע) — since it is in construct state (דבוק) with the word that follows it, that is to say 'firmament of heavens,' therefore it is pointed with a hatef vowel. And likewise 'harvest' (קציר), when it is in construct state, it is written ״עד כלות קציר השעורים וקציר החטים״. We already said above: ויבדל אלהים בין האור ובין החשך — but the exact end of the night and the beginning of the day was not yet known except by the sun's rising, and likewise the exact end of the day and the beginning of the night was not known except by the sun's setting and the emergence of the stars — to distinguish between the beginning of the day and the beginning of the night." "And they shall be for signs and for appointed times — as it is written concerning Hezekiah: ״זה לך האות מאת ה׳״ and so on, ״הלך הצל עשר מעלות״ and so on — see, the sun was a sign for him. And it is written: ״ונתתי מופתים בשמים ובארץ דם ואש״ and so on. And it is written: ״מאותות השמים אל תחתו״." "And for appointed times — from the course of the moon, which renews itself every twenty-nine and a half days, the appointed times of the year and the dating of documents are fixed, as it is written: ״עשה ירח למועדים״." "And for days — for from the emergence of the stars to the emergence of the stars is one day." "And years — the four seasons of the year constitute a complete year."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:17:06.951396563Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}